{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3780","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3780","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3780\",\"parent_revision\":\"722b963cfecd9d5dcc318556a31c9ab073f3a591\",\"root_revision\":\"56a9da4cb65fd42e430f980a9045bcaf61d93f51919b3f1d7d043fc06f76b1bb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe repository fast test suite passes but emits 144 warnings. Observed categories include MCP logging deprecations, Typer option deprecations, and PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning from dh_paths hanging-stub threads leaking into later dispatch-schema tests. Warning output obscures regressions and contradicts the repository validation policy that warnings should be resolved or explicitly scoped.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:48:59.457994Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: The full fast suite passes while emitting 144 warnings in three categories.\\nevidence: Bounded `uv run pytest` completed with `6591 passed, 54 skipped, 10 xfailed, 144 warnings`; summary grouped 44 MCPDeprecationWarning, 96 Typer DeprecationWarning, and 4 PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning emissions.\\nsource: local bounded reproduction on 2026-09-21.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: FastMCP client logging emits a deprecation under the installed 4.0.2 behavior.\\nevidence: Warning-as-error reproduction failed at `server.py:2609` -> `ctx.info` -> `fastmcp/server/context.py:1357` with `MCPDeprecationWarning: The logging capability is deprecated as of 2026-07-28 (SEP-2577)`. FastMCP 4.0.0 documents support for the 2026-07-28 protocol and deprecation/removal of server push-era capabilities.\\nsource: https://gofastmcp.com/changelog.md and installed FastMCP 4.0.2 runtime traceback.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Typer 0.27.0 warns whenever `is_flag` or `flag_value` is non-None.\\nevidence: Upstream `OptionInfo.__init__` explicitly calls `warnings.warn` when either value is non-None; local source passes `is_flag=True` four times, and warning-as-error produces seven deterministic test failures in one affected file.\\nsource: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fastapi/typer/0.27.0/typer/models.py and https://typer.tiangolo.com/reference/parameters/.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Hanging-stub daemon threads escape their owning tests and raise in later tests.\\nevidence: The red-capable sequence failed later in `TestDispatchSpawn::test_spawn_end_to_end_single_wave` with an ExceptionGroup containing four `PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning` instances; every traceback ends at `test_dh_paths.py:337` after `dh_paths.py:122`.\\nsource: local warning-as-error reproduction on 2026-09-21.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:47:09.598875Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Eliminate full test suite warning output\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\nGoal: Remove every observed warning from the fast test suite by correcting each emitting code or test lifecycle.\\nConditions:\\n1. Warning categories and counts are reproducible | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Current FastMCP logging behavior is verified from primary upstream/runtime sources | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Current Typer option behavior is verified from primary upstream sources | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Thread-warning trigger and ownership are identified | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Affected systems and deterministic validation commands are known | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:49:50.583400Z</sub>\\n\\nType: recurring-pattern\\nRationale: Three independent obsolete or unmanaged lifecycle patterns produce the same validation failure class, and each repeats across multiple calls/tests.\\nAnalysis Method: 6-sigma category measurement plus evidence-chain root-cause analysis.\\nScenario Target: fast suite passes with 144 warnings -> fast suite passes with zero warnings and category-specific warning-as-error checks pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:48:06.198918Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: 13 files across MCP runtime/tests, migration CLIs/tests, and path-resolution tests.\\n\\n### Code - Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` - 15 `ctx.info`/`ctx.warning` calls invoke deprecated MCP client logging.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` - three boolean options explicitly pass unsupported `is_flag=True`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/verify_migration_fidelity.py` - one boolean option explicitly passes unsupported `is_flag=True`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` - timeout worker intentionally leaves unexpected exceptions to thread reporting; production behavior is valid, but tests must not leave their synthetic workers to raise after teardown.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` - asserts deprecated context logging and tool behavior.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_groom_sections.py` - exercises groom paths that emit context logging.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_frontend_parity_ops.py` - exercises logging-emitting MCP operations.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` - exercises logging-emitting sync scenarios.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_validator_escape_classification.py` - exercises logging-emitting pull/sync paths.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` - invokes the affected Typer CLI.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_verify_migration_fidelity.py` - invokes the affected Typer CLI.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths.py` - owns the delayed `_hang` stub and its cleanup lifecycle.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` - deterministic downstream collection point used by the thread-warning reproduction; no source change expected.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\nNone identified; user-visible CLI behavior is unchanged.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- `pyproject.toml` - strict warning behavior and dependency versions are validation context; no suppression or downgrade change permitted.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n1. Backlog MCP tool progress reporting -> FastMCP Context -> deprecated MCP logging capability.\\n2. MCP server tests -> in-memory FastMCP client -> warning collection.\\n3. Backlog migration CLI -> Typer option metadata -> CLI parser construction.\\n4. Migration fidelity CLI -> Typer option metadata -> CLI parser construction.\\n5. Migration CLI tests -> Typer runner -> repeated warning emission.\\n6. Git project-root timeout -> daemon worker thread -> queue handoff.\\n7. Hanging-path tests -> delayed synthetic exception -> pytest threadexception hook.\\n8. Dispatch tests -> later test activity long enough to collect escaped thread exceptions.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every listed producer corrected or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected consumer test updated\\n- [ ] No warning filters or dependency downgrades added\\n- [ ] CLI semantics retained\\n- [ ] Full bounded fast suite reports zero warnings\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed while validating #3778\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"aa18035146318cdf733f987e7c502eae573d93c2ea007ca8243f896887496887\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVwhgPg\"}"}